From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miguel Salinas <mikeys@me.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:12:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(durable): afterTools can end the run after the round

A run ends after a tool round only when every result asks to terminate. A host
that decides from the round as a whole (a call waiting for human input, a run
or spend budget, a node handing the conversation off) had to make every tool
return control.terminate, or replace the generation's tools phase.

afterTools now returns { end: true } to end the run after the round, as a
round whose every call asked to terminate does: no further request, inputs
settled done with the tool-calling answer, the final boundary, and afterRun
with reason terminate. Hooks are still all asked; any end ends the run.
